{"title":"Legendre's Formula","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Legendre's Formula</b> states that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed34e5c72cedebc54cb2a0a796114d3102431c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[v_p(n!)=\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty} \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{n}{p^i}\\right\\rfloor =\\frac{n-S_{p}(n)}{p-1}\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc3b48a549e5343cc60b70b5a370016e14fa66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_p(n!)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"48\" height=\"20\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=P-adic_valuation\" title=\"P-adic valuation\">p-adic valuation</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf12237888b9641a1d0c223a651adf5dfdf4327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sum\" title=\"Sum\">sum</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Digit\" title=\"Digit\">digits</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> when written in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base\" title=\"Base\">base</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Simpler_Explanation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Simpler Explanation</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Proofs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proofs</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Part_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Part 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Part_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Part 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098074e93772e9269ed42cbef6592ad6f894c3ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Using the first form of Legendre's Formula, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da419fbae6e7d19cc3af06fbfe52efd524596d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=27$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b803838ba4ded99f094071740c256527784b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c6a7d15207a6dce7e40f2c7368837994b32fcd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}e_2(27!)=&amp;\\left\\lfloor\\frac{27}{2}\\right\\rfloor+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{27}{2^2}\\right\\rfloor+\\left\\lfloor\\frac {27}{2^3}\\right\\rfloor+\\left\\lfloor\\frac{27}{2^4}\\right\\rfloor\\\\ =&amp;13+6+3+1\\\\ =&amp;23\\end{align*}\" width=\"309\" height=\"88\" />\nwhich means that the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098074e93772e9269ed42cbef6592ad6f894c3ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a24f0e971d4d99be77a3c4906ecd92d4496b7dcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Using the second form of Legendre's Formula, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da419fbae6e7d19cc3af06fbfe52efd524596d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=27$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b803838ba4ded99f094071740c256527784b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58b2d9adb4bbce121285fa7fb8e3e3de60b09dd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e_2(27!)=\\frac{27-S_2(27)}{2-1}=27-S_2(27)\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"39\" />\nThe number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> when expressed in Base-2 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f2de461a0a79a96e0a9c90b49e33583df885a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7ac15c7702679accbb0f35de4e50a5ad6680dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2(27)=1+1+0+1+1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29ff02cecf0f7492913d8ed4eafa752e4c7b28c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e_2(27!)=27-S_2(27)=27-4=23\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />\nwhich means that the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767b7dc4a8df95a9f8a0faa3bb155e7b49943407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098074e93772e9269ed42cbef6592ad6f894c3ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a24f0e971d4d99be77a3c4906ecd92d4496b7dcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Simpler_Explanation\">Simpler Explanation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Simpler Explanation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Basically, we can find out how many you can divide a factorial by a prime number before you get a remainder.\nNote that this is not a solution, but an explanation for those who are stuck on what this formula accomplishes. \n~AtomicBoy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proofs\">Proofs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Proofs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_1\">Part 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Part 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We use a counting argument.\n</p><p>We could say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076961bd49a1fb1261ba98b8d0a7669bf55ee146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_p(n!)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the number of multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0bced933416790cabd8af1c8a6993193fd90993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{p}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"31\" height=\"43\" />. But the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are only counted once, when they should be counted twice. So we need to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83ec58185a24904a9df5e5a7995fbaf1f57303c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{p^2}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"43\" height=\"45\" /> on. But this only counts the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/3814a4283bc25004bcab7459523e16c0f089b3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> twice, when we need to count them thrice. Therefore we must add a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a325abb97cb1661080ec9572409795f1a1dbb879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{p^3}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"43\" height=\"45\" /> on. We continue like this to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7cfe22beb73b7f93c59e399dc787d012eec2188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_p(n!)=\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty} \\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{n}{p^i}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"140\" height=\"53\" />. This makes sense, because the terms of this series tend to 0.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Part_2\">Part 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Part 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78e48c27ac9f6f70520cd0a8a6b98e4bdfd2544.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e_xe_{x-1}e_{x-2}\\dots e_0\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"11\" /> where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26ae315076f64895667486f0c8faaa5ea17b5d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are digits in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6f23436a505304b2eb128a45ac703ff856cfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> Then, the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c3884f6c6d59d1540a314452ba26530702b0ca22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{p^i}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"35\" height=\"43\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9edc87be652e14c3f4deb8a69e2c0ddafabbd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e_xe_{x-1}\\dots e_{i}.\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> Note that the infinite sum of these numbers (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076961bd49a1fb1261ba98b8d0a7669bf55ee146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_p(n!)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />) is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023b2ee74729fc447042ff2d2057d2bf418b5e93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{j=1}^{x} e_j\\cdot(p^{j-1}+p^{j-2}+\\cdots +1) &amp;= \\sum_{j=1}^{x} e_j \\left( \\frac{p^j-1}{p-1} \\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{x} e_jp^j -\\sum_{j=1}^{x} e_j}{p-1} \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{(n-e_0)-(S_p(n)-e_0)}{p-1} \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{n-S_p(n)}{p-1}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"442\" height=\"200\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer greater than 4 such that the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> zeros and the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c65c2a874b19bdb25e07737a8a098ccd4c292e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6582d1a31d1fd6bdab19f0d332c8d93adb9c66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> zeros. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> denote the sum of the four least possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />? (2015 AMC 10B Problem 23)</li></ul>\n<ul><li>How many zeros are at the end of the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d48ed7b060a90510dbdd4ac1daf83459b88dccad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50!$\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />?</li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230ef7f3b0e8399957624fab8cf665868e767db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4042}{2021}+\\binom{4043}{2022}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"147\" height=\"53\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a45ab72fb5ee3b1a1cc0340cb16fd8126c857b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\cdot 10^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers. What is the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />? (BorealBear)</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Find the sum of digits of the largest positive integer n such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> ends with exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> zeros. (demigod)</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre%27s_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/82473f22c7fb9801c406acd5eeeb23cbc33ac7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be numbers of factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9d913109f09f79aa0f9b8182f420dd409b69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m!$\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> (that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a53f4f376cdce99b719faf8b992416624717cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{b_m}|m!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a3f24b532edd509b18bf20a2ad082abe3895fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{b_m+1}\\nmid m!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />). Find the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9e1de5098cca3a85baedf515d3b32e3b4e52f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-b_m = 1990$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />. (Turkey TST 1990)</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032336\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU tim